```tsx
Sentry.captureException(error, {
  tags: error.digest ? { digest: error.digest } : undefined,
  extra: { digest: error.digest },
});
```

The digest is a property Next adds to the error, and Sentry doesn't pick it up on its own, so it's now sent as a tag (searchable, `digest:abc123`) and as extra data. I also show it on the error page as "Error id" so a customer can quote it to support. It's only the hash Next generates, not the server message, so nothing sensitive leaks.

