try {
  // fetch, createObjectURL, append <a>, click, remove
  setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 10_000);
} finally {
  setLoading(false);
}
```

The spinner was only cleared in a click listener added after `a.click()`, which Safari never fires for a detached anchor (Chrome happened to download anyway, but the spinner logic was wrong everywhere). Loading now always resets, the anchor is attached before clicking, the URL is revoked a bit later so Safari has time to start the download, and failed responses no longer save an error page as a PDF.

